text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', "Activated abilities of artifacts can't be activated.", "As Nevermore enters the battlefield, choose a nonland card name.\\nSpells with the chosen name can't be cast.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile X cards from your graveyard.\\nHarvest Pyre deals X damage to target creature.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.\\nCorpse Lunge deals damage equal to the exiled card's power to target creature.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile a creature card from your graveyard.\\nFlying', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile three creature cards from your graveyard.\\nFlying\\nYou may cast Skaab Ruinator from your graveyard.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, exile two creature cards from your graveyard.\\nTrample', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nAdd {R}{R}{R}.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nDraw two cards.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Howlpack of Estwald.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Krallenhorde Wantons.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Merciless Predator.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Rampaging Werewolf.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Gatstaf Shepherd.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Grizzled Outcasts.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Reckless Waif.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Tormented Pariah.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Ulvenwald Mystics.', 'At the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Villagers of Estwald.', "At the beginning of your end step, if Homicidal Brute didn't attack this turn, tap Homicidal Brute, then transform it.", 'At the beginning of your end step, you lose 1 life.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, create X 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens, where X is half the number of Zombies you control, rounded down.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, look at the top card of your library. You may reveal that card. If an instant or sorcery card is revealed this way, transform Delver of Secrets.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, return an instant or sorcery card at random from your graveyard to your hand.\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Charmbreaker Devils gets +4/+0 until end of turn.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may pay {2}{B}{B}. If you do, transform Stalking Vampire.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may transform Cloistered Youth.', 'Attacking creatures you control get +1/+0.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Instigator Gang.', 'Bane of Hanweir attacks each combat if able.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Bane of Hanweir.', 'Bloodcrazed Neonate attacks each combat if able.\\nWhenever Bloodcrazed Neonate deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', "Boneyard Wurm's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard.", 'Brimstone Volley deals 3 damage to any target.\\nMorbid — Brimstone Volley deals 5 damage instead if a creature died this turn.', 'Choose a permanent type. Return all cards of the chosen type from your graveyard to your hand.\\nFlashback {5}{G}{G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Choose one —\\n• Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n• Return two target Zombie cards from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Clifftop Retreat enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Mountain or a Plains.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}. That player discards a card.', "Counter target spell. If that spell is countered this way, exile it instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard.", "Counter target spell. Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Create a 1/2 green Spider creature token with reach for each creature card in your graveyard.\\nFlashback {6}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Create a token that's a copy of target creature you control.\\nFlashback {5}{U}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", 'Create thirteen tapped 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.\\nFlashback {7}{B}{B}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Create two 1/1 white Spirit creature tokens with flying.', 'Create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.\\nFlashback {5}{B}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Creature spells you cast cost {2} less to cast.\\nCreatures you control get -1/-1.', 'Creature tokens you control get +1/+1 and have vigilance.', 'Creatures you control enter the battlefield as a copy of Essence of the Wild.', 'Creatures you control gain protection from non-Human creatures until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +2/+0 until end of turn.\\nFlashback {2}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Creatures your opponents control get -4/-0 until end of turn.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Deathtouch\\nWhen Bitterheart Witch dies, you may search your library for a Curse card, put it onto the battlefield attached to target player, then shuffle.', 'Defender, protection from Zombies', 'Defender\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Hanweir Watchkeep.', 'Defender\\nCreatures with flying your opponents control get -1/-0.', 'Defender\\nManor Gargoyle has indestructible as long as it has defender.\\n{1}: Until end of turn, Manor Gargoyle loses defender and gains flying.', "Defender\\n{1}{U}: Put a hatchling counter on Ludevic's Test Subject. Then if there are five or more hatchling counters on it, remove all of them and transform it.", "Defender\\n{T}: Exchange your life total with Tree of Redemption's toughness.", 'Destroy all enchantments. You gain 1 life for each enchantment destroyed this way.', 'Destroy target Spirit or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact.\\nFlashback {G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Destroy target attacking creature.', 'Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater.', 'Destroy target land. Into the Maw of Hell deals 13 damage to target creature.', 'Destroy target land. You gain 4 life.', 'Destroy target non-Vampire, non-Werewolf, non-Zombie creature.', 'Destroy target noncreature permanent.', "Devil's Play deals X damage to any target.\\nFlashback {X}{R}{R}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", 'Diregraf Ghoul enters the battlefield tapped.', "Double strike\\nWerewolves you control have menace. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Terror of Kruin Pass.", 'Draw a card.\\nFlashback {2}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Draw two cards, then discard a card at random.\\nFlashback {2}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard gains flashback until end of turn. The flashback cost is equal to its mana cost.\\nFlashback {4}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Each other creature you control that's a Werewolf or a Wolf gets +1/+1.\\nAt the beginning of your end step, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Howlpack Alpha.", 'Each player chooses a creature they control. Destroy the rest.\\nFlashback {5}{W}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and has "{B}: Regenerate this creature."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and attacks each combat if able.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 and has flying.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+2 as long as it's a Human. Otherwise, it can't attack or block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +X/+X, where X is the number of creature cards in your graveyard.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-2.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -3/-0.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has flying.\\nPrevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by enchanted creature.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has intimidate. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", "Enchant creature\\nWhen Claustrophobia enters the battlefield, tap enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.', "Enchant player\\nAt the beginning of enchanted player's upkeep, Curse of the Pierced Heart deals 1 damage to that player or a planeswalker that player controls.", "Enchant player\\nAt the beginning of enchanted player's upkeep, that player exiles two cards from their graveyard.", "Enchant player\\nAt the beginning of enchanted player's upkeep, that player mills two cards.", 'Enchant player\\nCreatures enchanted player controls attack each combat if able.', 'Enchant player\\nCreatures enchanted player controls get -1/-1.', 'Enchant player\\nWhenever a creature deals combat damage to enchanted player, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature.', 'Equipped creature can\'t be blocked by Vampires or Zombies.\\nEquipped creature has "{T}, Sacrifice Blazing Torch: Blazing Torch deals 2 damage to any target."\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Equipped creature gets +1/+0.\\nWhenever equipped creature blocks or becomes blocked by a Vampire, destroy that creature. It can't be regenerated.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", "Equipped creature gets +1/+2 and has hexproof. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nEquip {3}", 'Equipped creature gets +2/+0.\\nAs long as equipped creature is a Human, it gets an additional +1/+0.\\nEquip {2}', 'Equipped creature gets +3/+0.\\nAs long as equipped creature is a Human, it has lifelink.\\nEquip {3}', 'Equipped creature gets +4/+2.\\nEquip—Sacrifice a creature.', 'Equipped creature has first strike and gets +X/+0, where X is the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard.\\nEquip {2}', 'Equipped creature has first strike.\\nAs long as equipped creature is a Human, it gets +1/+1.\\nEquip {1}', 'Equipped creature has flying.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Exile a creature card from your graveyard and pay its mana cost: Create a token that's a copy of that card. Activate only as a sorcery.", 'Exile target card from a graveyard.\\nFlashback {W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Exile target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature.\\nFlashback {5}{B}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'First strike, vigilance\\nProtection from Vampires, from Werewolves, and from Zombies', 'First strike\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Ironfang.', 'First strike\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Kruin Outlaw.', 'First strike\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Village Ironsmith.', "First strike\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Abattoir Ghoul this turn dies, you gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhen Village Bell-Ringer enters the battlefield, untap all creatures you control.', 'Flash\\nDeathtouch', 'Flash\\nWhen Snapcaster Mage enters the battlefield, target instant or sorcery card in your graveyard gains flashback until end of turn. The flashback cost is equal to its mana cost. (You may cast that card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Flying', 'Flying, first strike', 'Flying, haste\\nWhenever Falkenrath Marauders deals combat damage to a player, put two +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying\\nAs long as Dearly Departed is in your graveyard, each Human creature you control enters the battlefield with an additional +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Flying\\nAs long as you control a Human, Angelic Overseer has hexproof and indestructible.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, return target Spirit card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, target player draws a card and loses 1 life.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may pay {2}{B}{B}. If you do, transform Screeching Bat.', 'Flying\\nMorbid — At the beginning of each end step, if a creature died this turn, destroy target non-Demon creature.', 'Flying\\nOther Spirit creatures you control get +0/+1.', 'Flying\\nOther Spirit creatures you control get +1/+0.', 'Flying\\nOther Vampire creatures you control get +2/+2.\\n{T}: Create a 2/2 black Vampire creature token with flying.', "Flying\\nSturmgeist's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.\\nWhenever Sturmgeist deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.", "Flying\\nVampire Interloper can't block.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Balefire Dragon deals combat damage to a player, it deals that much damage to each creature that player controls.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Falkenrath Noble or another creature dies, target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Flying\\nWhenever another creature dies, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', 'Flying\\n{1}{R}: Olivia Voldaren deals 1 damage to another target creature. That creature becomes a Vampire in addition to its other types. Put a +1/+1 counter on Olivia Voldaren.\\n{3}{B}{B}: Gain control of target Vampire for as long as you control Olivia Voldaren.', "Flying\\n{1}{U}: Mirror-Mad Phantasm's owner shuffles it into their library. If that player does, they reveal cards from the top of that library until a card named Mirror-Mad Phantasm is revealed. The player puts that card onto the battlefield and all other cards revealed this way into their graveyard.", "Flying\\n{2}: Target player mills a card. Mindshrieker gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the milled card's mana value.", 'Flying\\n{T}: Create a 2/2 black Vampire creature token with flying.\\n{B}: Transform Bloodline Keeper. Activate only if you control five or more Vampires.', "Flying\\n{U}: Return Lantern Spirit to its owner's hand.", 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap it. It gains trample and haste until end of turn.', "Galvanic Juggernaut attacks each combat if able.\\nGalvanic Juggernaut doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nWhenever another creature dies, untap Galvanic Juggernaut.", 'Geistflame deals 1 damage to any target.\\nFlashback {3}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Grimgrin, Corpse-Born enters the battlefield tapped and doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nSacrifice another creature: Untap Grimgrin and put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nWhenever Grimgrin attacks, destroy target creature defending player controls, then put a +1/+1 counter on Grimgrin.", 'Haste\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Manor Skeleton.', "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nInvisible Stalker can't be blocked.", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nWhenever Geist of Saint Traft attacks, create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying that's tapped and attacking. Exile that token at end of combat.", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nWhenever a creature dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Lumberknot.", 'Hinterland Harbor enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Forest or an Island.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', "If a Zombie you control would deal combat damage to a player, instead that player mills that many cards.\\nWhenever a creature card is put into an opponent's graveyard from their library, exile that card and create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.", 'If an effect would create one or more tokens under your control, it creates twice that many of those tokens instead.', 'If equipped creature would deal combat damage, it deals double that damage instead.\\nIf another creature would deal combat damage to equipped creature, it deals double that damage to equipped creature instead.\\nEquip {2}', 'If you would draw a card while your library has no cards in it, you win the game instead.', 'Indestructible\\nWhenever Creepy Doll deals combat damage to a creature, flip a coin. If you win the flip, destroy that creature.', "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)", "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Gatstaf Howler.", "Intimidate (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or creatures that share a color with it.)\\nSacrifice Brain Weevil: Target player discards two cards. Activate only as a sorcery.", 'Isolated Chapel enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Plains or a Swamp.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)', 'Look at the top four cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.\\nFlashback {6}{B} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Mikaeus, the Lunarch enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Mikaeus.\\n{T}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Mikaeus: Put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control.', 'Morbid — When Hollowhenge Scavenger enters the battlefield, if a creature died this turn, you gain 5 life.', 'Morbid — When Morkrut Banshee enters the battlefield, if a creature died this turn, target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.', 'Morbid — When Woodland Sleuth enters the battlefield, if a creature died this turn, return a creature card at random from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Morbid — {T}, Tap two untapped creatures you control: Create a 5/5 black Demon creature token with flying. Activate only if a creature died this turn.', 'Night Revelers has haste as long as an opponent controls a Human.', "Orchard Spirit can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.", 'Other Human creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Mayor of Avabruck.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.\\nFlashback {1}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.\\nFlashback {7}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nMorbid — Somberwald Spider enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it if a creature died this turn.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nFlashback {3}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\nFlashback {4}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", 'Return target exiled card with flashback you own to your hand.', 'Return two cards at random from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Reveal the top four cards of your library. Put all land cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'Rolling Temblor deals 2 damage to each creature without flying.\\nFlashback {4}{R}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Scourge of Geier Reach gets +1/+1 for each creature your opponents control.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\nMorbid — You may put that card onto the battlefield instead of putting it into your hand if a creature died this turn.', "Stromkirk Noble can't be blocked by Humans.\\nWhenever Stromkirk Noble deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.", 'Sulfur Falls enters the battlefield tapped unless you control an Island or a Mountain.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Tap up to two target creatures.\\nFlashback {1}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', "Target creature you control fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", "Target creature you control gets +1/+1 and gains hexproof until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)", 'Target opponent loses 3 life.\\nFlashback {5}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Target opponent sacrifices a creature. You gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", 'Target player mills three cards.\\nFlashback {1}{U} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Target player reveals their hand. You choose a nonland card from it. Exile that card.', 'Target player shuffles up to three target cards from their graveyard into their library.\\nFlashback {G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature on the battlefield.\\nBlasphemous Act deals 13 damage to each creature.', 'Trample', 'Trample\\nAttacking creatures you control get +3/+0.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Wildblood Pack.', 'Trample\\nMorbid — Festerhide Boar enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it if a creature died this turn.', "Trample\\nSplinterfright's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in your graveyard.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, mill two cards.", 'Trample\\nWhen Moldgraf Monstrosity dies, exile it, then return two creature cards at random from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Trample\\n{1}{R}: Feral Ridgewolf gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Transform all Humans. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn by creatures other than Werewolves and Wolves. (Only double-faced cards can be transformed.)', 'Unbreathing Horde enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each other Zombie you control and each Zombie card in your graveyard.\\nIf Unbreathing Horde would be dealt damage, prevent that damage and remove a +1/+1 counter from it.', 'Untap target creature. It gets +2/+4 and gains reach until end of turn. (It can block creatures with flying.)', "Up to two target creatures can't block this turn.\\nFlashback {3}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)", 'Vampire creatures you control get +2/+0 and gain first strike until end of turn.', "Vigilance\\nGeist-Honored Monk's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures you control.\\nWhen Geist-Honored Monk enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 white Spirit creature tokens with flying.", 'Vigilance\\nWhenever another creature you control dies, you may transform Thraben Sentry.', "Werewolf creatures you control get +1/+0 and have trample.\\nSacrifice Full Moon's Rise: Regenerate all Werewolf creatures you control.", 'When Armored Skaab enters the battlefield, mill four cards.', "When Crossway Vampire enters the battlefield, target creature can't block this turn.", 'When Doomed Traveler dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'When Elder Cathar dies, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control. If that creature is a Human, put two +1/+1 counters on it instead.', "When Fiend Hunter enters the battlefield, you may exile another target creature.\\nWhen Fiend Hunter leaves the battlefield, return the exiled card to the battlefield under its owner's control.", 'When Garruk Relentless has two or fewer loyalty counters on him, transform him.\\n[0]: Garruk Relentless deals 3 damage to target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power to him.\\n[0]: Create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.', "When Geistcatcher's Rig enters the battlefield, you may have it deal 4 damage to target creature with flying.", 'When Ghoulraiser enters the battlefield, return a Zombie card at random from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Mausoleum Guard dies, create two 1/1 white Spirit creature tokens with flying.', 'When Pitchburn Devils dies, it deals 3 damage to any target.', 'When Slayer of the Wicked enters the battlefield, you may destroy target Vampire, Werewolf, or Zombie.', "When Witchbane Orb enters the battlefield, destroy all Curses attached to you.\\nYou have hexproof. (You can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control, including Aura spells.)", 'Whenever Ashmouth Hound blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Ashmouth Hound deals 1 damage to that creature.', 'Whenever Hamlet Captain attacks or blocks, other Humans you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Whenever Kessig Cagebreakers attacks, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token that's tapped and attacking for each creature card in your graveyard.", 'Whenever Selhoff Occultist or another creature dies, target player mills a card.', 'Whenever Stromkirk Patrol deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Whenever a Vampire you control deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Whenever a nontoken creature you control dies, put a slime counter on Gutter Grime, then create a green Ooze creature token with "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to the number of slime counters on Gutter Grime."', 'Whenever another Human creature dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Village Cannibals.', 'Whenever another Human enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on Champion of the Parish.', 'Whenever another creature dies, Rage Thrower deals 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'Whenever another creature with power 2 or less enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {1}. If you do, draw a card.', 'Whenever another creature you control dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Unruly Mob.', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, defending player reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a land card. The creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each card revealed this way. That player puts the revealed cards into their graveyard.\\nEquip {2}', 'Whenever you cast a spell from your graveyard, Burning Vengeance deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Woodland Cemetery enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Swamp or a Forest.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'You gain 2 life for each creature card in your graveyard.\\nFlashback {2}{G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'You may have Evil Twin enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it has "{U}{B}, {T}: Destroy target creature with the same name as this creature."', 'You may pay {0} rather than pay the mana cost for Zombie creature spells you cast.', '[+1]: Create a 1/1 black Wolf creature token with deathtouch.\\n[−1]: Sacrifice a creature. If you do, search your library for a creature card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\n[−3]: Creatures you control gain trample and get +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of creature cards in your graveyard.', '[+1]: Each player discards a card.\\n[−2]: Target player sacrifices a creature.\\n[−6]: Separate all permanents target player controls into two piles. That player sacrifices all permanents in the pile of their choice.', "{1}, Sacrifice Traveler's Amulet: Search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", "{1}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain life equal to the sacrificed creature's toughness.", "{1}, {T}, Discard a card: Put a study counter on Grimoire of the Dead.\\n{T}, Remove three study counters from Grimoire of the Dead and sacrifice it: Put all creature cards from all graveyards onto the battlefield under your control. They're black Zombies in addition to their other colors and types.", '{1}, {T}: Tap target non-Human creature.', '{1}{R}: Kessig Wolf gains first strike until end of turn.', '{1}{U}, {T}: Create a 2/2 blue Homunculus creature token, then sacrifice a creature.', '{1}{W}, Sacrifice Selfless Cathar: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{1}{W}, Sacrifice Silverchase Fox: Exile target enchantment.', "{2}, {T}: Target player exiles a card from their graveyard. If it's a creature card, you gain 2 life.", '{2}{G}: Darkthicket Wolf gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', "{3}, {T}: Target player puts the bottom card of their library into their graveyard. If it's a creature card, you create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.", '{3}{G}: Target creature gets +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the number of creatures you control.', "{3}{R}: Choose any target, then mill three cards. Heretic's Punishment deals damage to that permanent or player equal to the highest mana value among the milled cards.", '{G}: Regenerate Ulvenwald Primordials.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Ulvenwald Primordials.', '{R}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: Skirsdag Cultist deals 2 damage to any target.', '{R}, {T}: Nightfall Predator fights target creature. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if a player cast two or more spells last turn, transform Nightfall Predator.', '{T}, Mill a card: Add {C}. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{U}{B}, {T}: Target player mills three cards.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{G}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}{B}{R}, {T}: Stensia Bloodhall deals 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ghost Quarter: Destroy target land. Its controller may search their library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{W}{U}, {T}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{X}{R}{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +X/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {W}.', '{T}: Daybreak Ranger deals 2 damage to target creature with flying.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, if no spells were cast last turn, transform Daybreak Ranger.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card. If a creature card is discarded this way, untap Civilized Scholar, then transform it.', '{T}: Each player mills a card.']
flavor: ['". . . and embrace the ancient ferocity of the undying Wild."', '"A responsible king walks among his subjects."', '"All that concerns me is the vampires\' sense of smell and those freezing Nephalian nights."', '"And then I realized we all have skeletons on the inside. Why wait until the bodies are dead to control them?"\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"As long as we can utter a prayer or lift a weapon, we have the power to fight back."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"At least this one still has arms and legs. Well, most of its legs."\\n—Enslow, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Avacyn has deserted you. I welcome your devotion in her stead."', '"Avacyn\'s protection is everywhere. From the holy church to the sacred glade, all that we see is under her blessed watch."', '"Be careful in your hunt. The clever little creature can steal your wards and lead you right into the werewolf\'s den."\\n—Britta, midwife of Gatstaf', '"Bury your dead deep. The boars are hungriest while the corpse is still warm."\\n—Paulin, trapper of Somberwald', '"By the law of Avacyn, the following thoughts, words, and deeds are henceforth disallowed."', '"Civilization is fertilizer."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"Come. Bring your brothers. Tonight, you feast on living flesh."\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Do not flatter Fate. It did not guide you into my clutches tonight. That was all my doing."', '"Do not touch a drop. Not yet. I want to watch this so-called slayer\'s last crisis of faith."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"Don\'t be afraid when you hear the wolves howl. Be afraid when you don\'t hear them at all."\\n—Saint Trogen, the Slayer', '"Either I know just the spell I need, or I\'m about to."', '"Garl, adjust the slurry dispensers. Garl, fetch more corpses. Garl, quit crying and give me your brain tissue. If he doesn\'t stop being so rude, I\'m quitting."', '"Ghoulcallers trying to get in, geists trying to get out . . . . This duty is never dull."', '"Hey lads, the moon\'s rising. All the better to watch him beg for mercy."', '"Hold tight. I\'ve got a surprise for them."', '"Holy places are no longer sanctuary from death, and death is no longer sanctuary from anything."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"I can make you dance to my tune like a puppet, your very blood eager to obey."\\n—Olivia Voldaren', '"I heard her talking in her sleep—pleading, shrieking, snarling. It was not my daughter\'s voice. That is not my daughter."\\n—Ekatrin, elder of Hanweir', '"I often think on how excited they must feel to be chosen as my prey."', '"I stand for every cobbler, tanner, and fool in this town—and they stand for me."', '"I would fear this fight, bloodsucker, were I alone."', '"I\'d rather take on a neckbiter or moonhowler any day. Oh well, looks like I\'m going to end up parrying with empty air half the night."\\n—Saint Trogen, the Slayer', '"I\'ve learned to trust my dogs\' instincts. When they\'re calm, I\'m calm. And when they get nervous, I get my crossbow."\\n—Hinrik of House Cecani', '"If I fail to offer myself, we will surely be overrun. My fate would be the same."', '"If you must go out at night, bring a mob."\\n—Master of the Elgaud Cathars', '"If you\'re not having fun, what\'s the point of living forever?"', '"In these halls there is no pass or fail. Your true test comes with the first full moon."', '"Innocent thorns can fill the air with your bloodscent. Don\'t stray from the path."\\n—Elmut, crossway watcher', '"Is it hopeless? When wave upon wave of our dead return as mindless flesh-eaters to claw upon Thraben\'s walls? We\'re too busy cutting them down to indulge ourselves in such philosophical foppery."\\n—Mikaeus, the Lunarch', '"It always amazes me what perfectly good things people throw away."\\n—Ludevic, necro-alchemist', '"Just look at him, groveling on all fours! What a pathetic—uh-oh."', '"Let go your grudges, or risk wandering the bogs forever in a murderous rage."\\n—Hildin, priest of Avacyn', '"Let those idiot priests tremble! A new era in unlife begins here and now. Oglor, raise the lightning vane!"\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"Living creatures seldom impress me. But I like this one."\\n—Uta Falkenrath', '"Looks like it\'s going to be a quiet night."', '"May you and all your kin waste and wither until your clan is no more!"', '"May your veins weep, and may every vampire take notice."\\n—Stensian curse', '"Me, angry? Of course not. Thanks to my research, I\'m above such petty emotions now."', '"Moonlight has a way of showing all things as they truly are—for better or for worse."\\n—Zilla of Lambholt', '"My faith is stronger than fang, claw, or mindless hunger."', '"My greatest hope is that you will surpass me in every way, consigning my name to some forgotten corner of history."', '"Never forget our ancestors. They have not forgotten us."\\n—Mikaeus, the Lunarch', '"No matter how many I kill, there are always more to hunt. It makes me smile just to think about it."', '"No one chooses to be stitched together into a skaab. If it could speak, it would beg for its own destruction."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"Nobody\'s seen the Lady of Videns for years. Poor dear, no companions at all in that old castle."\\n—Yonda of Gavony', '"Oglor create life, Oglor take it away. Oglor god! . . . until Master return."', '"Oh mighty Griselbrand, Scourge of the Heedless World, gladly I consume myself for thee!"', '"Pick not the rotten fruit, but neither touch the best. Leave those as an offering for our unseen guests."\\n—Radwick, farmer of Gatstaf', '"Priests, hunters, slayers—to arms! The enemy approaches!"', '"Some lament these haunted times, but I\'m a geistflame-tank-half-full kind of person."', '"Some see a coastal disaster. I see a fully-stocked seagraf."\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Stone and thought fade into ruin. Only the wind in the leaves will endure."\\n—Tomb inscription', '"Surely you know the joy of the hunt, my furry friend. My kind of hunt just takes a different form than yours."', '"The best skaab are more powerful and more beautiful than the sum of their parts."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"The church looks down on binding spirits into armor, but now I can look down on them."\\n—Dierk, geistmage', '"The darkness crawls with vampires and ghouls, but we are not without allies."\\n—Mikaeus, the Lunarch', '"The demons don\'t care if we mutter niceties and act out ceremonies. Just kill him."\\n—Bishop Volpaig, servant of Griselbrand', '"The living are born small and weak. The dead rise ready to serve. The choice is obvious."\\n—Gisa, ghoulcaller of Gavony', '"The mist whispers to those who know it to be more than a mundane fog."', '"The panic is amusing, but the real fun comes when the spell passes and the villagers start looking for a scapegoat."\\n—Ludevic, necro-alchemist', '"The protective wards of the church have weakened, and no one can tell us why. It\'s time to look to our own defenses."\\n—Gregel, militia leader', '"The time for grief is over. The time for retribution has begun."', '"The wolves no longer hunt just to feed. They kill for sport, or for some madness behind their eyes."\\n—Elmut, crossway watcher', '"There will come a time when the only prey left will be each other."\\n—Ulrich of Krallenhorde Pack', '"They put bars on these noble beasts and then wonder why werewolves target our towns."', '"They won\'t be winning any beauty pageants, but they\'ll do the trick."\\n—Enslow, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"This abomination never belonged in our world. I\'m merely setting it free."\\n—Dierk, geistmage', '"This is the price of being last in the food chain. We must keep our places of beauty hidden away instead of displayed for all to see."\\n—Hildin, priest of Avacyn', '"Thraben\'s pleas fall on deaf ears. Ours do not."', '"Three heads, six arms, and some armor grafts are better than . . . the normal numbers of those things."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"To show geists pity is to prolong their agonies. Whether they know it or not, they seek the Blessed Sleep, and we are to give it to them."\\n—Mikaeus, the Lunarch', '"Unfortunately, all my test animals have died or escaped, so I shall be the final subject. I feel no fear. This is a momentous night."\\n—Laboratory notes, final entry', '"What cannot be destroyed will be bound."\\n—Oath of Avacyn', '"What is worse than a wolf in sheep\'s clothing?"\\n—Wolfhunter\'s riddle', '"What some call obsession, I call the quest for perfection."', '"Whatever did this is near. Death reversion has not yet occurred. Be alert!"', '"Who says werewolves are the only ones who can hunt as a pack?"\\n—Kolman, elder of Gatstaf', '"With this ritual, we cast aside our fragile humanity . . ."', '"Within blood is life. Within life is fire. Within fire is the path to our masters\' glory!"', '"Yes, I\'m alone. No, I\'m not worried."', '"You don\'t find many old werewolf hunters."\\n—Paulin, trapper of Somberwald', '"You\'d best move along, human. Our palates are far less discerning than our master\'s."', "A child's porcelain doll went missing one night, as did a pair of kitchen shears and the town magistrate.", "A devil's hands are never idle.", "After seeing his life's work drip away, the mage decided it was a good time to go crazy.", 'After several frustrating experiments, the visionary Ludevic realized he needed to create a monster that fed on torch-wielding mobs.', 'After werewolves slaughtered the citizenry of Hollowhenge, other creatures moved in.', 'All crave the Blessed Sleep. Few receive it.', 'Animated by geists fused in its oak, it hungers for more life to add to its core.', 'As if anyone needed another reason to avoid dark, dank cellars.', "As sharp as its bearer's words of faith.", 'As the chapel was dragged under, the bell in the tower rang until the murky depths forever silenced its toll.', "Before she just wanted to snatch your purse; now she'll take the whole arm.", 'Before you travel the woods of Kessig, first get permission from those who died trying.', 'Bound to the square where she died, she calls out to those in danger—usually scaring them straight into the peril she warns of.', 'Corpses destroyed by fire form the most destructive geists.', 'Death has bound it with chains of past regrets. Forever it searches for atonement, each kindness removing a single link.', 'Death took his humanity but not his skill with the knife.', 'Deserted, but not uninhabited.', "Devils are demons' unearthly desires made flesh. Let loose on the world, they satisfy their mad craving for destruction in a whirlwind of chaos.", 'Each form she takes is an exploration of the senses.', 'Each morning, he repairs the front door.', 'Each night, he abandons the trappings of civilization.', "Estwald's citizens don't dislike outsiders—they taste just fine.", 'Even more than carrion, they crave the last words of the dying.', 'Farmers cut the trees and buried their dead. The dead rose up and killed the farmers. The trees grew back and strangled the dead.', 'Farmhands and priests mutter curses at the ragged thing; it unnerves more than just the crows.', 'Few entrances lead to where demons and devils lurk. Unfortunately, they occasionally open new ones.', 'For a ghoul, every village is a buffet and every disaster is a reunion.', 'For a moment his basest desires run free, unshackled by reason or conscience.', 'For the necro-alchemist, any puzzle can be solved with intelligence and harvested body parts.', 'From mortal hope immortal power springs.', 'He can deny his true nature for only so long.', 'He listens to every heartbeat, deciding which one of hundreds he will stop.', 'He relishes the devotion of his Skirsdag puppets and their belief that it will earn them immortality.', "He scans for wolves, knowing there's one he can never anticipate.", "He vowed he would never rest until he reached his destination. He doesn't know how right he was.", 'Her mind was quite gone, yet she spoke nothing but truth.', 'His mind whirled with grand plans, never thinking of what might happen if he were to succeed.', 'Hopes and prayers can carry the same force as swords and torches.', 'If it comes for you, die boldly or die swiftly—for die you will.', "If there's anything a werewolf hates, it's a collar—especially Avacyn's Collar, the symbol of her church.", 'In Gavony wishing is taken as a sign of weakness, yet the wells usually brim with silver.', 'In life, they were a motley crew: farmers, lords, cutpurses, priests. In death, they are united in singular, benevolent purpose.', "In places where the sea meets the trees, it's easy to forget the darkness that rules most of Innistrad.", 'In the forest villages of Kessig, parents feed their children wormwood and other bitter herbs, hoping to make them less palatable to things that roam the night.', 'In the remote corners of Kessig, protection is found in secret powers unknown to the Church of Avacyn.', 'Innistrad is a place where dreams invade the mind and mere shadows exact a terrible toll.', 'Innistrad pyromancers find their best raw materials in the fury of the dead.', 'It comes off as easily as your own skin.', 'It hides the face and protects the soul.', "It's not just the wind. It's not all in your head. And it's *definitely* something to worry about.", 'Its fiery paws make it easy to track, which is very useful when you want to go in exactly the opposite direction.', 'Its venom sacs are long gone, but its crushing strength is somehow greater than ever.', 'Kidnappers caught in Havengul are given two choices: languish in prison or become rat catchers. The smart ones go to prison.', 'Let moss grow over gargoyles\\n—Gavony saying meaning "forget painful memories"', 'Literally made for battle.', 'Lungs dried to parchment wheeze blasphemies within a cage of bleached bone.', "Magical etchings turned a whittler's tool into a wolfhunter's weapon.", "Many peasants secretly admire vampires' glamour and elegance—until they witness a moment of pure bloodlust.", 'Marella was delighted. The ball had attracted so many suitors for her daughter, including that handsome stranger. She wondered where the two were now . . . .', "Mist is the geists' sorrow. Wind is their pain. Fire is their vengeance.", "Moorlanders speak in awe of the priests' talent for arriving just in time to drive off the wicked things that prowl the ravished parish.", 'Nature abhors a zombie.', 'Never a word. Never a warning. Only the sound of hoofbeats along the crossways, and the screams of the avenged.', 'No slinking in the dark for them, no luring whispers. They claim their prey in the speed and glory of the hunt.', 'Not content to nudge vases and chill drawing rooms, some geists muster spectral armies to claw at the hearts of the living.', 'Not every church is a place of faith.', 'Not everyone can have a sword of blessed silver. Not everyone needs one, either.', 'Nothing could break it but the fall.', 'On Innistrad, death is just a career change.', 'Outside the safety of Thraben, there is little distinction between tool and weapon.', 'People only say "I\'m sure it was nothing" when they\'re sure it was something.', 'Seen as unsavory, the hunters were never allowed in town—until one night they vanished.', 'She endures without Avacyn but secretly asks each soul she guides if it has seen her.', 'She wanted to inspire terror wherever she went. The demons happily granted her wish.', 'Shiny polished silver can ward off many creatures, but it attracts others.', 'Six feet of earth muffled his cries.', "Skirsdag cultists meet behind a waterfall's curtain and plot with demonic forces.", 'Some have endured the horrors of Innistrad by becoming the worst monsters of all.', 'Some lycanthropes wish they could abandon their weak human shapes and revel in the power of the wolf.', 'Some priests speak in whispers of the Helvault, a silver prison of unpurged evils.', 'Sometimes death comes knocking. Sometimes it tears down the walls.', 'Stensian vampires encourage spiders near their manors so they can rob the webs.', 'Stensian villagers mourned the loss of human life. Thraben vampire slayers mourned the loss of living wood.', 'Survival of the purest.', 'Technically he never left his post. He looks after the wolf wherever it goes.', "Thanks to Havengul's thriving illegal market for corpses, the shovel that interred a body during the day is usually the same one digging it out at night.", 'The bat has such clarity of hearing that simple sounds become symphonies.', "The bell's chime heralds the rise of the unhallowed from the grave and the fall of their victims into the earth.", 'The boot prints became paw prints, and they led right back into town.', 'The border between life and death is as thin as a layer of topsoil.', "The crueler vampires' idea of free-range farming.", 'The demon Griselbrand dared to stand against Avacyn, earning him the loathing of thousands and the admiration of a few.', "The executioner's tree in Thraben Cathedral holds the power to absolve more than the souls of the hanged.", "The fiend tormented them by recounting the girl's memories, as if some part of her remained inside that twisted shell.", 'The first step to peace is to learn how to forget.', 'The heron is the symbol of the archangel Avacyn. The fact that such spirits still fly gives the church hope that its founder may one day return.', 'The ingenuity of goblins, the depravity of demons, and the smarts of sheep.', 'The land knows no difference between the graves of commoners and nobles.', 'The only thing it likes more than discovering a pit of bones is adding to it.', "The path back to the world of the living is murky and bewildering. A geist may not even realize that it's terrifying its own loved ones.", 'The revelry ends when the supply of fresh ingenues runs dry.', 'The rider set off into the eerie mist, swaddled in armor and laden with amulets.', 'The rigs were outlawed except in Nephalia, where malign spirits are as plentiful as crazed inventors.', 'The same magic that lets geists pass through our realm can force them out of it.', 'The secrets she carried could have saved many lives, but they quietly drowned with her.', 'The spirit cares nothing for the crimes or triumphs of the slain. It shelters all beneath its stormy cloak.', 'They call it "stitcher\'s anesthesia," a spell to deaden the senses while the mad doctors begin their grisly work.', 'Those who only believe themselves infected with lycanthropy can be as dangerous as those who really are.', 'Though the old holy wards and roadside shrines have begun to fail, faith in Avacyn still holds true power.', 'Unbreakable and unappetizing, the crab grows uninterrupted, sometimes to the size of a cottage and beyond.', 'Vampires of the Markov bloodline pride themselves on their exquisite taste in fashion, art, and "wine of the vein."', 'Vampires think of themselves as the indisputable nobility of Innistrad, able to do as they please. There are few who can prove them wrong.', 'Visiting a shrine at the start of a journey makes the traveler more likely to finish it.', 'Wander too far into the wild and it may take you for its own.', "Werewolf slayers don't know for certain how werewolves are created. So they kill all the wolves, just to be safe.", 'When a werewolf changes for the first time, that first howl is said to echo through the wilds till moonset.', "When demons open a path to your front door, it's time to move.", 'When the moon rises and the bloodlust takes hold, nothing matters but the kill.', 'Where cathars learn to fight not only demons and vampires, but ignorance as well.', 'Whether he actually exists is in question, but the terror she feels is excruciatingly real.', 'While elder vampires select their meals with care, the newly sired frenzy at the first whiff.', "With Thraben's army recalled to its city walls, outlying villages were left to fend for themselves.", "You can always tell the evil one by the dagger he's sticking in you.", 'You can spot a werewolf-infested town by its lack of butcher shops.', "You don't want to see his trophy room."]
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Alan Pollack', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony Jones', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Austin Hsu', 'Bud Cook', 'Charles Urbach', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Donato Giancola', 'Drew Baker', 'E. M. Gist', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Erica Yang', 'Eytan Zana', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jana Schirmer & Johannes Voss', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'John Stanko', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Mark Evans', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Nils Hamm', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Scott Chou', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Winona Nelson']
